<title>FRANCE: New York top origin for ADP Jan-Oct cargo imports.</title>
<headline>New York top origin for ADP Jan-Oct cargo imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Paris airports authority, the Aeroports de Paris (ADP), said New York was the top airport gateway for imports to Charles de Gaulle and Orly Airports in the first ten months of 1996.</p>
<p>The top ten originating airport gateways for January-October ADP imports in tonnes with percentage changes on Jan-Oct 1995.</p>
<p>  1  New York	  32,530 tonnes   down  7.0pct</p>
<p>  2  Chicago	   24,228 tonnes   up   13.1</p>
<p>  3  Hong Kong	 16,538 tonnes   down  4.6</p>
<p>  4  Los Angeles     13,904 tonnes   down  6.7</p>
<p>  5  Tokyo	     13,525 tonnes   down 14.5</p>
<p>  6  Montreal	  11,103 tonnes   down  0.1</p>
<p>  7  Miami		6,270 tonnes   down  3.8</p>
<p>  8  Casablanca	 4,982 tonnes   down 10.3</p>
<p>  9  Dubai		4,509 tonnes   down  1.7</p>
<p>  10 Johannesburg     4,430 tonnes   up   20.4</p>
<p>- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel:+44 171 542 7706 Fax+0171 542 5017</p>
</text>
